<title>AUSTRALIA: FOCUS-Murdoch's News surges in Australia.</title>
<headline>FOCUS-Murdoch's News surges in Australia.</headline>
<byline>Bernard Hickey</byline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rupert Murdoch's News Corp Ltd roared back into favour on Thursday as investors re-rated the global media group after it announced two deals to buy and sell U.S. television assets worth US$3 billion.</p>
<p>News' shares surged as much as 38 cents or 6.5 percent to a new three month high of A$6.25 in hectic morning trade.</p>
<p>Analysts and brokers welcomed News' decision to sell its American Sky Broadcasting (ASkyB) satellite assets to the Primestar group of pay television operators for US$1.1 billion.</p>
</text>
